/.bsp/
/null/
/.idea/

# `project/` is BUILD SOURCE and must be committed: `project/plugins.sbt` supplies every
# symbol build.sbt uses from a plugin (dynverVTagPrefix, idePackagePrefix, MdocPlugin,
# ScalaUnidocPlugin, mimaPreviousArtifacts, ProblemFilters, sonatypeCredentialHost, mdocIn)
# and `project/build.properties` pins sbt itself to 1.10.11.  Without them a fresh clone
# cannot even load the build.
#
# This file used to ignore `/project/` wholesale.  That was harmless only by accident: the two
# source files were tracked *before* the rule was added, and a gitignore entry does not affect
# an already-tracked file.  Any NEW file there -- the `project/Dependencies.scala` that a
# growing build eventually wants -- would have been silently untracked, and the breakage would
# have surfaced as a failing CI run on someone else's clone rather than here.
#
# Only the build OUTPUT under project/ is ignored, and the unanchored `target/` below already
# covers `project/target/` and `project/project/target/`.
project/project/
# UNANCHORED since the 5.2 phase 1.1 module split: the leading slash matched the root
# target/ only, so core/target/ and repl/target/ -- and any future module's -- would have
# been committed. Matches a directory named `target` at any depth, the sbt convention.
target/

# Jekyll documentation-site build artifacts (see .github/workflows/pages.yml)
/_site/
/docs/_site/
/docs/.jekyll-cache/


# Claude Code's per-machine settings. `.claude/settings.json` is the shared, committable one and
# is deliberately NOT ignored; `settings.local.json` holds facts true only of this working copy —
# today the `additionalDirectories` reach into `../Leonardo_Training`, whose path exists on this
# machine and nowhere else. Committing that would also invert the dependency in the record: the
# library would be publishing a claim about courses that depend on *it*, which is the repo-level
# form of "core depends on no domain".
/.claude/settings.local.json

# The local planning-and-record documents. `Done.md` was NOT here until 2026-09-30 and was
# ignored only by `.git/info/exclude` -- which is per-clone and never shared, so on any fresh
# clone it would have appeared as untracked and been one `git add .` away from being committed.
# CLAUDE.md states as a design fact that `Done.md` is not tracked ("so it is not an alternative
# to the changelog"); that fact was resting on a file git does not distribute.
/CLAUDE.md
/.sbtopts
/ToDo.md
/DesignNotes.md
/Done.md

# Python bytecode from the .github/scripts guards (issue 2.8); regenerated on every run.
__pycache__/

# Claude Code's scratch utilities. Never build or test scripts -- those belong to sbt and to
# .github/scripts, which ARE committed because CI runs them. This directory is one-off tooling
# (a ToDo.md re-ordering pass, a one-time scan) that must not reach the repository.
/.claudetools/
/DevResources/
/METHODOLOGY.md
